.he "wc (1)                       8/16/26                       wc (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
wc
- word count
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
wc [ -lwc ] [ name ... ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Wc counts the lines, words and characters in the named files, or in
the standard input when no name is given.  A word is a run of
characters that are not space, tab or newline.  When more than one
file is counted a line of totals is printed too.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
OPTIONS
.in +5
.br
.in +10
.ti -10
-l	Count lines only.

.ti -10
-w	Count words only.

.ti -10
-c	Count characters only.

.in -10
.sp
The default is -lwc; the counts print in the order lines, words,
characters.
